{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Abraham hearkened to My voice.</b> When I tested him." "<b>And kept My charge.</b> decrees drawn far from the warnings in the Torah — such as secondary prohibitions of forbidden relations, and the rest of Sabbath (Yevamot 21)." "<b>My commandments.</b> matters that even had they not been written, are fitting to be commanded — such as robbery and bloodshed." "<b>My statutes.</b> matters against which the evil impulse and the nations of the world object — such as eating pork and wearing shaatnez — which have no reason, but the decree of the King and His statutes upon His servants." "<b>And My Torah.</b> to bring the oral Torah, halachah given to Moses at Sinai (Bereshit Rabbah)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:38.085070406Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}